SUMMARY:Graduate Events: Alexis (Lan) Wang\, University of California\, S
 anta Barbara - “Homeland Echoes: Chinese Immigrant Fertility and the R
 elaxation of China's One-Child Policy”
LOCATION:North Hall 2111
DESCRIPTION:Speaker: Alexis (Lan) Wang\, University of California\, Santa
  Barbara\nTitle: “Homeland Echoes: Chinese Immigrant Fertility and the
  Relaxation of China's One-Child Policy”\n\nWe study whether China's 2
 011 to 2021 fertility-policy relaxations affected childbearing among Mai
 nland-born and U.S.-born Chinese mothers in the United States. Using res
 tricted-use U.S. Vital Statistics natality records and Poisson pseudo-ma
 ximum-likelihood event studies\, we compare Mainland-born mothers with H
 ong Kong- and Taiwan-born mothers. In California\, second-order births a
 mong Mainland-born mothers with Chinese partners peak in 2017 at 4.3 tim
 es their 2011 level relative to the comparison group. Through 2018\, inc
 reases are later and smaller with non-Chinese partners and smaller for U
 .S.-born Chinese mothers. These patterns suggest that origin country pol
 icy changes continue to influence childbearing in Chinese immigrant comm
 unities. JEL Classification Codes: J13\, J15\, J61\, O15\, Z13\n\nhttps:
 //econ.ucsb.edu/events/all/2026/advancement-candidacy-presentation-homel
 and-echoes-chinese-immigrant-fertility-and
URL:https://econ.ucsb.edu/events/all/2026/advancement-candidacy-presentat
 ion-homeland-echoes-chinese-immigrant-fertility-and
