SUMMARY:Graduate Events: Komal Trishna\, University of California\, Santa
  Barbara - “More Seats\, Same Services: Council Size and Local Public 
 Goods in India”
LOCATION:North Hall 2212
DESCRIPTION:Speaker: Komal Trishna\, University of California\, Santa Bar
 bara\nTitle: “More Seats\, Same Services: Council Size and Local Publi
 c Goods in India”\n\nI study village councils (gram panchayats) in Mah
 arashtra\, India\, where statutory population thresholds add two council
  members. Using a multi-cutoff regression discontinuity design with 2011
  Census population and 2020 administrative data on 27\,152 councils\, I 
 find no detectable effect of additional representatives on drinking wate
 r\, sanitation\, or health infrastructure. At the 1\,500 threshold\, cou
 ncil size rises by 29 percent and the design is most precise\; there\, I
  rule out effects on a summary index of service delivery larger than 0.2
  standard deviations. The results suggest that adding representatives wi
 thout adding authority or resources does not change what local governmen
 ts deliver. Keywords: Representation\, Decentralization\, Local governme
 nt\, Public Goods JEL Classification Codes: H41\, H75\, H70\, O18\, D72\
 n\nhttps://econ.ucsb.edu/events/all/2026/advancement-candidacy-presentat
 ion-more-seats-same-services-council-size-and-local
URL:https://econ.ucsb.edu/events/all/2026/advancement-candidacy-presentat
 ion-more-seats-same-services-council-size-and-local
